## Note

A freeform written record about something: `title`, a markdown `body`, an `author`, `createdAt`, and `about`, the card it annotates. `about` is `linksTo(CardDef)`, so a note can attach to anything. Without a title, the card title falls back to a cleaned excerpt of the body, so quick notes still list legibly.

```ts
import { Note } from '@cardstack/catalog/cards/service-desk/note';

export class SessionNote extends Note {
  static displayName = 'Session Note';
  @field session = linksTo(() => Session);
}
```

Extending it is the intended use: a domain note keeps the body, author and `about` link, and adds the link its domain needs.

The linked example is a note on the checkout 502s case.

### Non-goals

Not a message: no recipient, thread or visibility flag; Thread covers conversation. Not a document: no sections or attachments. Edit history is the platform's, not the card's.
